  "question": {
    "text": "If the area bounded by <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;sq. units&nbsp;(where <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></math>), then the value of&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
